/* book Worked example 2: Q: A surface-emitting LED has radiance B0 = 100 W cm⁻² sr⁻¹ and emitting radius 35 µm. It is butted against a step-index fiber with core radius 25 µm, NA = 0.20 and core index 1.48, across a thin air gap. Find (a) the total power emitted, (b) the power coupled into the fiber before Fresnel loss, (c) the coupling efficiency in dB, and (d) the power left after Fresnel reflection at the fiber face.
   1. Radii in cm, to match B0: rs = 35 µm = 3.5×10⁻³ cm; a = 25 µm = 2.5×10⁻³ cm.
   2. Total power: Ps = π²rs²B0 = 9.870 × (3.5×10⁻³)² × 100 = 9.870 × 1.225×10⁻⁵ × 100 = 1.209×10⁻² W = 12.1 mW.
   3. rs > a, so P = π²a²B0NA² = 9.870 × 6.25×10⁻⁶ × 100 × 0.04 = 2.467×10⁻⁴ W = 0.247 mW.
   4. Efficiency: η = 0.247/12.1 = 0.0204, the same as (25/35)² × 0.20² = 0.510 × 0.04. In dB: −10 log₁₀(0.0204) = 16.9 dB.
   5. Fresnel at the fiber face: R = ((1.48 − 1)/(1.48 + 1))² = (0.48/2.48)² = 0.0375; the face passes 0.9625 (a 0.17 dB loss).
   6. Power in the fiber: 0.247 mW × 0.9625 = 0.237 mW.
   Answer: Ps = 12.1 mW, the fiber takes 0.247 mW (η = 0.0204, a 16.9 dB coupling loss), and 0.237 mW remains after Fresnel reflection. */
